session's `# prompt-template:` names the override path, so the\n@@ -72,8 +86,9 @@ substitution is visible in the telemetry rather than only in the launch flags.\n \n def render():\n     \"\"\"The catalogue's full text. Pure — takes no arguments and touches no\n-    state beyond reading the shipped templates, so `--check` and the write path\n-    cannot disagree about what \"current\" means.\n+    state beyond reading the shipped templates and composed fragments, so\n+    `--check` and the write path cannot disagree about what \"current\" means.\n+    Raises `prompts.PromptError` when a composed fragment cannot be read.\n \n     Implements: SR-146, LLR-164\n     \"\"\"\n@@ -87,7 +102,21 @@ def render():\n         )\n         for key, filename, slot_names, digest in prompts.catalog_rows()\n     ]\n-    return HEADER + \"\\n\".join(rows) + \"\\n\" + FOOTER\n+    fragments = [\n+        \"| [{file}]({file}) | `{digest}` | `{{{slot}}}` |\".format(\n+            file=filename, digest=digest, slot=slot\n+        )\n+        for filename, slot, digest in prompts.fragment_rows()\n+    ]\n+    return (\n+        HEADER\n+        + \"\\n\".join(rows)\n+        + \"\\n\"\n+        + FRAGMENTS\n+        + \"\\n\".join(fragments)\n+        + \"\\n\"\n+        + FOOTER\n+    )\n \n \n def main(argv=None):\n@@ -104,7 +133,13 @@ def main(argv=None):\n         \"--print\", dest=\"show\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"print, write nothing\"\n     )\n     args = ap.parse_args(argv)\n-    text = render()\n+    try:\n+        text = render()\n+    except prompts.PromptError as exc:\n+        # Before any write, so the previous catalogue stands; and for `--check`\n+        # too, so an unreadable source is a red gate rather than a green one.\n+        print(\"gen_prompt_catalog: {}\".format(exc), file=sys.stderr)\n+        return 1\n     if args.show:\n         print(text, end=\"\")\n         return 0\n@@ -120,8 +155,9 @@ def main(argv=None):\n             print(\"gen_prompt_catalog: fresh ({} prompts).\".format(text.count(\"\\n| `\")))\n             return 0\n         print(\n-            \"gen_prompt_catalog: {} is STALE — a template changed and the \"\n-            \"catalogue did not. Run `python scripts/gen_prompt_catalog.py` \"\n+            \"gen_prompt_catalog: {} is STALE — a template or composed fragment \"\n+            \"changed and the catalogue did not. Run \"\n+            \"`python scripts/gen_prompt_catalog.py` \"\n             \"and commit the result.\".format(\n                 CATALOG.relative_to(prompts.KIT.parent)\n                 if CATALOG.is_relative_to(prompts.KIT.parent)\ndiff --git a/project-trajectory/scripts/prompts.py b/project-trajectory/scripts/prompts.py\nindex 2e6153f7..7c3a80fa 100644\n--- a/project-trajectory/scripts/prompts.py\n+++ b/project-trajectory/scripts/prompts.py\n@@ -58,10 +58,14 @@ Contract IF-097: the prompt LOADER. `KIT_PROMPTS` is the declared key-to-file ma\n     shipped template.\n Contract IF-098: the generated prompt catalogue's row source. `catalog_rows()`\n     returns `(key, file, slots, digest)` for every shipped prompt whose file is\n-    present, sorted by key, and the catalogue reads nothing else — so the\n-    document cannot disagree with the loader about what ships or with what\n+    present, sorted by key, and the catalogue reads nothing but it and\n+    `fragment_rows()` — so the document canno
[... byte cap hit — full stream in out/run-logs/ ...]
overed it. It takes that finding's option (a).\n\n- [MEANING] LLR-162 Detail -> `load`, `fill`, `digest` and `preflight` over the shipped templates; the catalogue's freshness gate; the per-session fingerprint -> the same, PLUS: `KIT_FRAGMENTS` declares each composed fragment and the slot it fills; `fragment_rows` reads each through the shared `_read_body`, digests its normalized text, and raises `PromptError` for an absent, unreadable or empty fragment, never omitting it or digesting it as empty -> not the same: a new declared set, a new row source, and a refusal rule with no skip (unlike a template, whose absence `preflight` reports). BLESSED: the code matches clause for clause. `_read_body` is now the one read that templates and fragments share. `fragment_rows` builds no skip path. `adjudicate_brief` takes the home's filename from `KIT_FRAGMENTS`, so the catalogue and the composing brief name one file. Read upward, this is what SR-146 asks: every prompt source a launched brief carries is a shipped, reviewable file listed by digest in a freshness-gated catalogue.\n- [MEANING] LLR-164 Detail -> `render` is pure over the shipped templates; `--check` compares normalized line endings; the file is a trunk-owned generated artifact -> `render` is pure over the templates AND the composed fragments; the catalogue carries a Composed fragments table (file, digest, filled slot); a `PromptError` from either source fails generation before any write and fails `--check`, leaving the previous catalogue in place and the gate red -> not the same: new catalogue content, a new staleness trigger, and a new failure mode, since an unreadable source now reds the gate where before nothing read it. BLESSED: `main` catches `PromptError` around `render()` before the write and the check branch, returning 1 and writing nothing, which is exactly the stated failure behaviour. The template table is unchanged, so no existing digest moves. `--check` reports fresh across 12 prompts.\n- [MEANING] TC-192 Method -> render exercised directly; every key and digest listed; the committed file fresh; a template edit moves its digest but a line-ending difference does not; the wired step reds on a template edit -> the same, PLUS: an edit to the composed home reds `--check`; a line-ending difference in the home keeps it green; an absent, undecodable or notes-only home fails generation and `--check` while the written catalogue stays byte-identical; the wired step reds on a home edit and greens after regeneration -> not the same: new verification is owed. BLESSED: reading down, every new clause of LLR-162 and LLR-164 has its test, including the \"no omission, no empty digest\" refusal and the \"previous catalogue stands\" guarantee. This session, the selected tests in `test_routing_and_prompts.py` and `test_generated_freshness_wiring.py` gave 10 passed, including both wired-step cases (2 passed).\n\nObservation, not a return. The digest is taken over the fragment's body after its notes block is stripped, which is the same rule the templates follow. A change to text the brief does not compose, such as the home's `# ` title line before the first `## ` section, still stales the catalogue. That errs toward staleness, never toward a silent miss, which is the right direction for a freshness gate.\n\nVERDICT: MEANING rows=3\n\nAftermath: the LLR/TC rung is released and all three rows are blessed. The act re-attests LLR-162, LLR-164 and TC-192 in its own commit.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
