and raises a named `PromptError`; `fill` refuses an unknown slot and an unfilled declared slot; `digest` normalizes line endings before hashing; `preflight` turns a missing template into a launch-time refusal. `KIT_FRAGMENTS` declares each composed fragment and its slot; `fragment_rows` reads each through the shared `_read_body`, digests its normalized text, and raises `PromptError` when it is absent, unreadable or empty rather than omitting it or digesting it as empty. `gen_prompt_catalog.py` renders the catalogue with a `--check` freshness gate, and `agent_common.prompt_fingerprint` records the rendered result per session beside the template's own name.\""," rationale = \"\"\"Normalizing before hashing is not cosmetic: the same template checked out CRLF on Windows and LF on POSIX is the same prompt, and a telemetry field that said otherwise would report a model change on every clone.\"\"\"","-test_refs = \"TC-157\"","+test_refs = \"TC-157; TC-192\""," status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 5"]},{"oldStart":1669,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1669,"newLines":7,"lines":[" title = \"The generated prompt catalogue and its freshness gate\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/gen_prompt_catalog.py\""," code_symbol = \"render/main\"","-detail = \"\"\"`render` is PURE — it takes no arguments and reads only the shipped templates — so `--check` and the write path cannot disagree about what \"current\" means. `--check` compares on NORMALIZED line endings, for the same reason the digest is taken that way: a CRLF checkout is not a stale catalogue. The file is declared in `docs/stack.ini [generated]` as kind `promptcatalog`, so the trunk lane owns it and a work branch never commits it.\"\"\"","+detail = \"`render` is PURE — it takes no arguments and reads only the shipped templates and composed fragments — so `--check` and the write path cannot disagree about what \\\"current\\\" means. The catalogue carries template rows and a Composed fragments table with each fragment's file, digest and filled slot; a `PromptError` from either source fails generation before any write and fails `--check`, leaving the previous catalogue in place and the gate red. `--check` compares on NORMALIZED line endings, for the same reason the digest is taken that way: a CRLF checkout is not a stale catalogue. The file is declared in `docs/stack.ini [generated]` as kind `promptcatalog`, so the trunk lane owns it and a work branch never commits it.\""," rationale = \"\"\"A generated artifact nobody re-generates is a document that lies, and a lying catalogue is worse than none: it invites the operator to conclude the wrong thing about the session they are debugging. Same contract `gen_arch_map --check` and `gen_skills_index --check` hold.\"\"\""," test_refs = \"TC-192\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-882\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":1960,"oldLines":13,"newStart":1960,"newLines":13,"lines":[" phase = 5"," "," [test.TC-192]","-verifies = [\"SR-146\", \"LLR-164\"]","+verifies = [\"SR-146\", \"LLR-162\", \"LLR-164\"]"," level = \"Unit\"","-method = \"\"\"gen_prompt_catalog.render is exercised directly rather than read. test_the_catalogue_lists_every_shipped_prompt_with_its_digest asserts that the rendered text contains every prompts.KIT_PROMPTS key and every prompts.catalog_rows() digest. test_the_catalogue_on_disk_is_FRESH runs catalog.main([\"--check\"]) against the committed file and asserts exit 0 - the freshness gate LLR-164 names. test_a_template_edit_moves_its_digest_and_so_the_catalogue asserts that a real text edit moves the digest while a bare line-ending difference does not. tests/test_generated_freshness_wiring.py::test_prompt_catalog_step_reds_when_a_template_changes drives the wired [step:] enforcer end to end over a bootstrapped scaffold: edit a template, assert the commit-floor step reds, run gen_prompt_catalog.py, then assert it goes green.\"\"\"","+method = \"\"\"gen_prompt_catalog.render is exercised directly rather than read. test_the_catalogue_lists_every_shipped_prompt_with_its_digest asserts that the rendered text contains every prompts.KIT_PROMPTS key and every prompts.catalog_rows() digest. test_the_catalogue_on_disk_is_FRESH runs catalog.main([\"--check\"]) against the committed file and asserts exit 0 - the freshness gate LLR-164 names. test_a_template_edit_moves_its_digest_and_so_the_catalogue asserts that a real text edit moves the digest while a bare line-ending difference does not. test_an_edit_to_the_composed_question_home_stales_the_catalogue edits the composed home and sees `--check` red; test_a_line_ending_difference_in_the_home_is_not_an_edit keeps it green; and test_an_unreadable_home_fails_generation_and_the_check covers an absent, undecodable or notes-only home, requiring generation and `--check` to fail while leaving the written catalogue byte-identical. tests/test_generated_freshness_wiring.py::test_prompt_catalog_step_reds_when_a_template_changes and test_prompt_catalog_step_reds_when_the_composed_question_home_changes each drive the wired [step:] enforcer end to end over a bootstrapped scaffold: edit their source, assert the commit-floor step reds, run gen_prompt_catalog.py, then assert it goes green.\"\"\""," tier = \"Full\""," expected = \"Satisfies the acceptance folded into LLR-164 (parent SR-146)\""," automated = \"Yes\"","-evidence = \"\"\"tests/test_routing_and_prompts.py::test_the_catalogue_lists_every_shipped_prompt_with_its_digest; tests/test_routing_and_prompts.py::test_the_catalogue_on_disk_is_FRESH; tests/test_routing_and_prompts.py::test_a_template_edit_moves_its_digest_and_so_the_catalogue; tests/test_generated_freshness_wiring.py::test_prompt_catalog_step_reds_when_a_template_changes\"\"\"","+evidence = \"\"\"tests/test_routing_and_prompts.py::test_the_catalogue_lists_every_shipped_prompt_with_its_digest; tests/test_routing_and_prompts.py::test_the_catalogue_o