{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CftzdcLE7bqx6fV6Chvzo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three rows are **MEANING**, and I blessed all three and re-anchored them myself, since the LLR/TC rung is released. This lane closes the gap I flagged in WI-854's sitting 001: the composed question home (`spine-questions.md`) is now listed by digest in the prompt catalogue.\n\n**Verdict** (`aa05b2a4`, trailer `WI: WI-882`, file `docs/reviews/wi-882/001-ADJUDICATE-a8883e2.md`, `VERDICT: MEANING rows=3`):\n- **LLR-162:** composed fragments are now declared in `KIT_FRAGMENTS` and read through the same reader the templates use. A missing, unreadable or empty fragment is refused with a `PromptError`; it is never skipped or digested as empty. `adjudicate_brief` takes the home's filename from that same declaration, so the catalogue and the brief name one file.\n- **LLR-164:** the catalogue gains a \"Composed fragments\" table, and an edit to the home now makes `--check` fail. An unreadable fragment fails generation before anything is written, so the previous catalogue stays in place and the check fails. The template table is unchanged, so no existing digest moved.\n- **TC-192:** the new tests cover every new clause: an edit fails the check, a line-ending-only difference doesn't, and a missing, undecodable or notes-only home fails both generation and `--check` without changing the written file. The wired commit-floor step fails on a home edit and passes again after regenerating.\n\n**Checks run:** 10 selected tests passed, including both wired-step cases, and `gen_prompt_catalog.py --check` reports the catalogue fresh.\n\n**One observation, not a return:** editing parts of the home the brief never uses, such as its title line, still marks the catalogue stale. For a freshness check that's the safe direction to err.\n\n**Re-attestation** (`03431efd`, act 98): `intake.py snapshot --reattests LLR-162,LLR-164,TC-192` copied both registries with nothing refused. I edited no registry cells."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":374974,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":632},"output_tokens":690,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a511e73-e906-4589-9f31-ae73f8534ed7","uuid":"872e2cf3-f000-4d71-a9d2-7d19be22b4ee","timestamp":"2026-10-10T18:01:35.221Z","request_id":"req_011Cftzdc6pwYnZxmXhMVsqD"}
